I must say I think of the opening game / middle game distinction as being
when the focus shifts from simple survival to character optimisation
(hence a combat wombat may be in the middle game very soon); the endgame
(as distinct from the Endgame) starts as soon as Rodney is dead.

Mind you, since doing a bulk ID exercise often effects that change in the
game, I suspect we actually put the divide in much the same place.

The only exceptions I'd list are that wands can nearly all be sorted out
as soon as you get them (you touch on this) and if you have an altar
potions are much easier to sort out with price-ID and judicious
experimentation (and observation, obviously) than scrolls are; uncursed
amulets go on right away; uncursed rings are tried for a turn; price-ID
spellbooks and read any uncursed ones you can't fail at; and really I
should write a spoiler about this, except I did. :-)
